1. Challenge Card – Commerzbank (zdjęcia 1–2)
Collabothon 2026 – Challenge Card
Challenge title: Finance Quest

Organisation: Commerzbank

Contact person for challenge topics:
- Sandra Fensterseifer
- Thomas Muth
- Anel Memic
Discord Channel for general questions: #Commerzbank
Current context
What does the current reality look like in the context of this challenge?

For many people, the barrier to making better financial decisions is not simply a lack of information. Financial products can feel complex, and even after learning the basics, people may still hesitate to take action.

Meanwhile, the way people consume information is changing. Short, accessible, and engaging content is increasingly shaping expectations, while traditional learning formats can feel time-consuming and disconnected from real-life decisions.

Our challenge is to bridge the gap between financial knowledge and action, creating learning experiences that reduce complexity, build confidence, and empower people to take the next step.
Challenge
What is the problem / challenge in this area? What is not working properly / optimally?

How can we make financial learning engaging, relevant and actionable so that self-directed investors not only seek out financial knowledge, but feel confident enough to take the first step and apply what they learn?
Goal & expected change
What would you like to change or achieve by implementing the solution?

The goal is to help self-directed investors understand financial concepts and build confidence in applying them. The proposed approach can be a gamified platform or a similar engaging learning format using missions, challenges, and real-world scenarios.
Expected outcomes & benefits
- demonstrable prototype showing a complete learning “mission”.
- An explanation of the target learner and learning objective.
- A demonstration of how the experience supports understanding and engagement.
Fit with theme
How does the proposed challenge fit the Collabothon 2026 theme “Innovations for all generations”?

Make financial learning relevant across life stages by reflecting different goals, investment horizons, financial circumstances, and levels of experience.
